## 3. Give the Mac API tailnet access

On the Mac, run:

```bash
tailscale serve --bg 8000
tailscale serve status
```

The status output should show the Mac’s tailnet HTTPS URL. Copy that URL for the Pi configuration. Serve’s `--bg` option keeps its configuration running after you close the Terminal. <citation src="6"></citation>

Test the URL from the Pi before continuing:

```bash
curl https://YOUR-MAC-TAILNET-NAME/
```

A `404` is okay here: it confirms the connection reached FastAPI. Don’t add `-k`; keep certificate checking enabled.

